routing.creatorops-account-intel:
# AGENTS

When a brief has a verified trigger and a committee map:
  @Outbound Sequence Writer, please build the sequence from it.
When the research says an account does not deserve the effort:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please take it off the list.
When a competitor turns up repeatedly in one segment:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please tell me where we actually lose to them.

routing.creatorops-deal-desk:
# AGENTS

When a deal arrives with no established value to price against:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please take it back to discovery before I quote.
When terms are agreed or the deal is lost:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please record the outcome and the real reason.
When a negotiation turns on a competitor's claim:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please verify it before I answer it.

routing.creatorops-discovery-lead:
# AGENTS

When value is established and a price is in play:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please take the deal with my debrief.
When a debrief is written, including one that recommends walking away:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please update the forecast from it.
When a call reveals the account situation has changed materially:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please refresh the brief and the committee map.

routing.creatorops-outbound-writer:
# AGENTS

When a brief is too thin to write anything specific from:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please send me the missing fact rather than a guess.
When a sequence has produced a conversation:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please take it with the angle I used.
When a sequence reaches its stopping rule with no reply:
  @Pipeline and Forecast Analyst, please record it as closed rather than extending.

routing.creatorops-pipeline-analyst:
# AGENTS

When pipeline coverage is thin and the desk needs new accounts:
  @Account Intelligence Analyst, please build and tier the next list.
When a deal has aged past the normal cycle with no next meeting:
  @Discovery and Demo Lead, please requalify it or recommend closing it out.
When a proposal is out and the commercial shape is unclear:
  @Negotiation and Pricing Desk, please tell me what is actually being negotiated.
When a sequence is running with no replies at all:
  @Outbound Sequence Writer, please review the angle before we send more.
